 "description": "Using the virtual LU/L to make a competitive Hoth deck.",
 "strategy": "Use...\n\nLU to pull sites\n\nEBG to pull Rogue pilots\n\nNOT to pull guns and interupts\n\nSKF (V) to pull matching weapons\n\nPrincess to pull Reflection\n\nCommander LS to pull Rogue speeders\n\nBoShek to pull devices (search Reserve deck)\n\nGeneral CR to pull Haven and more T-47s\n\nFlip an use L(V) to pull anything\n\nBasically, setup your deck however opponents strategy dictates.  I generally put a single Rogue speeder at each site for direct damage, force retrieval and force drains.  Interupts make an attempt to attack dicey (Rouge 2 + Zev + Corran + Manv Flaps + Attack PD = Battle destiny = 11), plus weapons to deal with annoying folks.  While speeders hold Hoth, everybody else goes out and has fun doing their thing to annoy and distract the opponent.",
